items.text:
do {
    // body — executes FIRST, at least once
    // update variable here
} while (condition);  // ← semicolon REQUIRED

Three essential components: (1) Body — the block of statements that execute first. (2) Condition — a boolean expression evaluated AFTER each body execution. (3) Update — inside the body, a statement that changes the loop variable toward making the condition eventually false. Forgetting the semicolon after while(condition) is a compile-time error — it is the single most common syntax mistake in do-while loops.

